    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess... but the \"process\" feels so exhausting though. like, if the end result is always just going to be total disorder and silence, isn't all this struggle just something we're doing to ourselves? it feels like we're fighting a war that's already lost. why is it considered \"beautiful\" to just struggle through something that's fundamentally doomed to disappear? it just seems more logical to just accept the equilibrium sooner rather than fighting it for no reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
